---
// src/pages/colocation.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Carrier-Neutral Colocation Sourcing (Racks to Cages) | InfraHub"
  description="Source carrier-neutral colocation space across major European, US, and Asian datacenter markets. Evaluate power density (5kW-40kW+), cooling, MMR cross-connects, and remote hands."
  canonicalPath="/colocation"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container service-container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <div class="header-badge-row">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-blue">Datacenter Facilities</span>
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Sourced</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="service-title">Carrier-Neutral Colocation Sourcing</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          Find and secure optimal datacenter space from quarter racks to private high-density cages across Europe, North America, and Asia. We evaluate power availability, PUE efficiency, carrier density in the MMR, and remote-hands response SLAs.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=colocation" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Colocation Sourcing</a>
          <a href="#power-density" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Review Density Factors</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Problem Solved -->
      <div class="content-section" id="power-density">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Facility Evaluation</span>
        <h2>Navigating Datacenter Sourcing Challenges</h2>
        <p>
          Legacy enterprise datacenters frequently lack the power density or cooling capacity required for modern NVMe storage arrays and GPU AI hardware. Sourcing colocation requires evaluating:
        </p>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Power Density per Rack</h3>
            <p>Moving beyond legacy 3kW-5kW allocations to modern 10kW-40kW+ circuits required for dense compute and AI workloads.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>True Carrier Neutrality</h3>
            <p>Access to open Meet-Me-Rooms (MMRs) with 20+ on-net fiber carriers to ensure competitive transit and wavelength pricing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>24/7 Smart Remote Hands</h3>
            <p>SLA-backed hardware replacement, optics cleaning, loopback testing, and serial console access by on-site engineers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Form Factors Available -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Space Allocation</span>
        <h2>Available Colocation Deployments</h2>
        <div class="colo-types-grid">
          <div class="colo-type-card">
            <h3>Quarter & Half Racks</h3>
            <p>Shared secure cabinets with dedicated power feeds and lockable partitions, ideal for regional POPs and edge routing gear.</p>
            <span class="type-spec">Power: 1kW - 3kW | 10U / 20U Space</span>
          </div>

          <div class="colo-type-card">
            <h3>Full 42U / 48U Cabinets</h3>
            <p>Dedicated enterprise enclosures with dual redundant A+B PDU circuits, hot/cold aisle containment, and biometric cabinet locks.</p>
            <span class="type-spec">Power: 5kW - 20kW | Full Isolation</span>
          </div>

          <div class="colo-type-card">
            <h3>High-Density AI / GPU Cages</h3>
            <p>Reinforced perimeter mesh cages engineered for high-density GPU clusters with rear-door heat exchangers or direct liquid cooling.</p>
            <span class="type-spec">Power: 25kW - 60kW+ per rack</span>
          </div>

          <div class="colo-type-card">
            <h3>Private Datacenter Suites</h3>
            <p>Custom-built dedicated datacenter halls with isolated electrical distribution, UPS redundancy, and dedicated physical access.</p>
            <span class="type-spec">Scalable: 50kW - 500kW+ halls</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- When Colocation Fits vs Bare Metal -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Facility selection</span>
        <h2>Colocation vs Managed Bare Metal</h2>
        <div class="fit-comparison-grid">
          <div class="fit-card fit-yes">
            <h3>When Colocation Fits</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You own custom, proprietary, or specialized hardware (e.g. FPGA, specialized GPU rigs, proprietary HSM security modules).</li>
              <li>You have a multi-year deployment horizon (36+ months) where CapEx hardware amortizes far below cloud OpEx.</li>
              <li>You require physical chain-of-custody compliance and dedicated audit-trail controls.</li>
              <li>You have in-house or contracted engineering staff to manage hardware lifecycles.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="fit-card fit-no">
            <h3>When Managed Bare Metal Is Better</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Zero Hardware CapEx:</strong> You prefer operational monthly billing without purchasing and depreciating physical servers.</li>
              <li><strong>Remote Sourcing:</strong> You lack local engineers to swap failed hard drives, RAM DIMMs, or power supplies.</li>
              <li><strong>Deployment Timing:</strong> Compare quoted rack, cross-connect, remote-hands, and hardware-delivery lead times when the schedule is critical; turn-up varies by facility and scope.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- How InfraHub Helps -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <div class="infrahub-role-card">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Facility Matching</span>
          <h2>How InfraHub Streamlines Colocation Sourcing</h2>
          <p>
            We maintain real-time relationships with wholesale and retail datacenter operators across Europe (Frankfurt, Amsterdam, London, Dublin), North America (Ashburn, Dallas, Silicon Valley), and Asia-Pacific (Singapore, Tokyo):
          </p>
          <div class="role-points-grid">
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Inventory & Power Audits</h3>
              <p>We verify real available power capacity, circuit lead times, and rack dimensions before you initiate RFP cycles.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Cross-Connect Transparency</h3>
              <p>We compare facility cross-connect recurring fees, which often represent 30%+ of the total monthly datacenter expenditure.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Direct Facility Contracts</h3>
              <p>You contract directly with the facility operator under their standard datacenter service agreements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2>Source Datacenter Colocation</h2>
        <p>Talk to our facility architects to identify available space and power in your target metropolitan market.</p>
        <a href="/lets-talk?service=colocation" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Colocation Availability</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-container { max-width: 1040px; }
  .service-header { text-align: left; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 0 64px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .header-badge-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .service-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .service-lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .service-hero-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .section-sub-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .content-section > p { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 780px; margin-bottom: 28px; }

  .problem-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .problem-card { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .problem-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .problem-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }

  .colo-types-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 640px) { .colo-types-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .colo-type-card { background-color: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 28px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; }
  .colo-type-card h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .colo-type-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .type-spec { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-teal); }

  .fit-comparison-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .fit-comparison-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .fit-card { border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 32px; }
  .fit-card h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .fit-card ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .fit-yes { background-color: var(--accent-teal-light); border: 1px solid rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.3); color: #0f766e; }
  .fit-yes h3 { color: #0f766e; }
  .fit-yes ul { color: #115e59; }
  .fit-no { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .fit-no h3 { color: var(--text-primary); }

  .infrahub-role-card { background-color: var(--bg-dark); color: #ffffff; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 44px 36px; }
  .infrahub-role-card h2 { color: #ffffff; margin: 12px 0 16px; }
  .infrahub-role-card > p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .role-points-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .role-points-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .role-point { background-color: transparent; border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); border-radius: 0; padding: 18px 0 0; }
  .role-point h3 { color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .role-point p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .service-footer-cta { padding: 40px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; gap: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
</style>
